739:
The following uses or conditions shall be and are hereby prohibited within wellhead protection zones, whether or not such use or condition may otherwise be ordinarily included as a part of a use permitted under section 32-276:
(1) Surface use or storage of hazardous material, expressly including commercial use of agricultural pesticides;
(2) Septic tanks or drainfields appurtenant thereto;
(3) Impervious surfaces other than roofs of buildings, and streets, driveways and walks serving buildings permitted under section 32-276;
(4) Sanitary landfills;
(5) Hazardous waste disposal sites;
(6) Stormwater infiltration basins;
(7) Underground storage tanks; and
(8) Sanitary sewer lines within 150 feet of a wellhead.
(Code 1996, § 34-35; Ord. of 5-1-1995, § 5)
